{"name":"Moonlight Sonata","hex":"#4e468b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"moonlight","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The light reflected from the Moon, which seems to emanate from it.","The silvery colour of the light reflected by the Moon."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To do a moonlight flit: to secretly leave premises without paying the rent, supposedly at night by the light of the Moon.","To do a moonlight flit: to secretly leave premises without paying the rent, supposedly at night by the light of the Moon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moonlight"},{"term":"sonata","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A musical composition for one or a few instruments, one of which is frequently a piano, in three or four movements that vary in key and tempo."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sonata"}],"entries":[{"title":"Moonlight Sonata (EP)","blocks":[{"text":"Moonlight Sonata  is the 2nd EP and the final release from American progressive metal band The Human Abstract. The EP was released on February 14, 2012, and is a cover of all three parts of Ludwig van Beethoven's \"Moonlight Sonata\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1e/The_Human_Abstract_Moonlight_Sonata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moonlight_Sonata_(EP)","wikidata":"Q17026204"},{"title":"Moonlight Sonata (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Moonlight Sonata is a 1937 British drama film directed by Lothar Mendes and written by E. M. Delafield and Edward Knoblock. The film stars Ignacy Jan Paderewski, Charles Farrell, Marie Tempest, Barbara Greene and Eric Portman. The film was released on 11 February 1937, by United Artists\nand re-released in 1943 as The Charmer (shortened)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/93/%22Moonlight_Sonata%22_%281937_film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moonlight_Sonata_(film)","wikidata":"Q18209283"},{"title":"Piano Sonata No. 14 (Beethoven)","blocks":[{"text":"The Piano Sonata No. 14 in C♯ minor, marked Quasi una fantasia, Op. 27, No. 2, is a piano sonata by Ludwig van Beethoven, completed in 1801 and dedicated in 1802 to his pupil Countess Julie \"Giulietta\" Guicciardi. Although known throughout the world as the Moonlight Sonata, it was not Beethoven who named it so. The title \"Moonlight Sonata'\" arose via imagery later proposed by the poet Ludwig Rellstab, which resonated with listeners."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Beethoven_Piano_Sonata_14_-_title_page_1802.jpg/330px-Beethoven_Piano_Sonata_14_-_title_page_1802.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Piano_Sonata_No._14_(Beethoven)","wikidata":"Q12008"},{"title":"Moonlight","blocks":[{"text":"Moonlight is light from the surface of the Moon, consisting mostly of reflected sunlight, and some earthlight."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Earthshine_Moon.jpg/330px-Earthshine_Moon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moonlight","wikidata":"Q1058800"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Manuscript_of_the_Piano_Sonata_No._14_in_C-sharp_minor_Op.27-2_by_Beethoven_%28trimmed%29.pdf/page1-500px-Manuscript_of_the_Piano_Sonata_No._14_in_C-sharp_minor_Op.27-2_by_Beethoven_%28trimmed%29.pdf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Manuscript_of_the_Piano_Sonata_No._14_in_C-sharp_minor_Op.27-2_by_Beethoven_%28trimmed%29.pdf/page1-1280px-Manuscript_of_the_Piano_Sonata_No._14_in_C-sharp_minor_Op.27-2_by_Beethoven_%28trimmed%29.pdf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&ut